# AI assistant files
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
*.claude

# Local TLS material (dev/test PKI - never commit private keys). The
# default location moved outside the repository (#598: make certs and the
# server both default to SEP2_CERT_DIR, or ~/tls). Ignored by what a file
# IS, not by what directory it sits in: a directory-name rule is what
# collided with internal/certs/, a source package, in the first place, and
# a bare `certs/` or `tls/` entry would do it again for either name, at
# any depth (test/certs/, e2e/certs/, deploy/certs/). *.key and *.pem
# catch stray key material wherever it lands, including under the new
# tls/ default, without needing to enumerate every directory name that
# could hold one.
*.key
*.pem
# The CSIP conformance test PKI is deliberately tracked (see
# test/csip/README.md and the fixtures entry below): device_chain.pem,
# device_key.pem and root_ca.pem under testdata/csip-pki/. Directory-scoped
# rather than per-file so a fixture added later here is exempted without a
# .gitignore edit. This only works while no ancestor of the path is itself
# excluded: git cannot re-include a file under a directory that is already
# ignored, so an entry like `testdata/` added anywhere in this file would
# silently swallow the exemption below it and the fixture would go back to
# ignored. Do not add one.
!testdata/csip-pki/**

# CSIP conformance fixtures. The SunSpec V1.2 test PKI is gitignored
# per workspace policy and provisioned out of band (see
# test/csip/README.md). Topology YAMLs (#52) ARE checked in.
test/csip/fixtures/*
!test/csip/fixtures/.gitkeep
!test/csip/fixtures/*.yaml

